      "problem": "What is the value of  ${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{3{log}_{2}\u2061({x}^{2})}{\\sqrt{2}x}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{2}\u2061({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{3{log}_{2}\u2061({x}^{2})}{\\sqrt{2}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{log}_{2}\u2061({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{2}^{4}u\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{4\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot (16-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
